WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.140
With a divine twist and one Hell of an ending,
the final season of Lucifer delivers an incredibly

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.830
emotional send-off for all our favourite characters.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:13.150
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video we'll be taking a deep dive into

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:17.390
the finale to uncover and explain all the
clues and details you might have missed.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:21.359
Plus we'll discuss whether a season 7 or spin-off
could still be possible.

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:23.660
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.690
Although Luci fought a battle to be the new
God, in Season 6 he finds himself full of

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:32.460
doubts about whether he's really the right
angel for the job.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.180
And by the end, he realises his true calling
isn't to rule on high, but to help redeem

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.620
the souls of the damned below.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.670
When he said Hell no longer needs a keeper,
it doesn't.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.190
It needs a healer.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.640
After all, who better to help those condemned
to Hell than Lucifer who'd lived there for

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.220
millennia in his own Hell Loop of sorts believing
it was his job to punish people?

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:57.690
It wasn't until he went to LA and began therapy
with Dr Linda that he was able to slowly deal

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.510
with his anger and self-loathing.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:04.540
It took him years to fully understand himself,
and during that time he almost transformed

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:08.289
entirely into a monstrous devil form at the
end of Season 4.

00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:12.511
His devil face, which we've seen since the
show began, was a crucial part of Luci's sense

00:01:12.511 --> 00:01:15.320
of guilt and self-hatred, as God explained
to his son.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.950
Why did you choose that face?

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.350
Deep down, that face is how you see yourself.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:24.450
So, when Lucifer sees his daughter Rory giving
in to her anger and manifesting her own devil

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:29.450
face against LeMec, he recognises it for what
it is and begs her not to give in to those

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:30.450
urges.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.110
Killing him won't change what he's done, but
it will change you.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:38.179
I know what it's like to be consumed by guilt,
by anger and self-hatred.

00:01:38.179 --> 00:01:43.450
As Rory later explains, Lucifer has a special
gift that troubled people like her can relate

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.450
to.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:49.170
When I looked in your eyes, I knew you understood
my anger and the guilt more than anyone else

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.170
could.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.350
And when Luci, Chloe and Rory realise that
it was his advice to Dan's ghost that helped

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:58.300
him finally ascend to Heaven,
Chloe explains that helping those who are

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.759
stuck within their own guilt-ridden Hell Loops
could be Lucifer's true purpose.

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:03.950
You can help everyone.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.179
Every Dan down in Hell who deserves another
chance.

00:02:07.179 --> 00:02:10.390
Luci agrees and thinks he'll be able do the
job part-time,

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:14.510
which does make some sense when you consider
that time in Hell moves differently so he

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:18.700
could be down there delivering hundreds or
thousands of years of therapy and only be

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.260
gone in Earth time for a few months.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:25.910
However, Rory explains that wouldn't be possible
because if Lucifer is there for her as a father

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.030
as she grows up,
she'll never become angry enough to time travel

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:33.540
to the past and help him arrive at this moment
of self-discovery about his ability to help

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.709
rescue millions of condemned souls in Hell.

00:02:35.709 --> 00:02:36.709
Everything that we've been through, it all
leads to what Dad just realized, that he needs

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:37.709
to help those lost souls.

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:39.680
We can't change anything, or he might never
get that idea.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.840
What Rory's describing is a type of time paradox
which you can pick apart if you start to think

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:50.209
about it too much, so I suggest for pure enjoyment
of the show to just go along with it.

00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:51.209
My advice?

00:02:51.209 --> 00:02:52.209
Don't overthink it.

00:02:52.209 --> 00:02:56.310
In fact, this Season 6 storyline with Chloe
and Lucifer's daughter Rory being crucial

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.959
to his ultimate destiny
fits nicely as one of the reasons he was so

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:04.079
insistent on bringing Chloe back from Heaven
at the end of Season 5.

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:05.110
It's not your time.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.400
You need to come back.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.530
There were also some theories at the end of
Season 5 that Chloe getting stabbed in the

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:14.360
stomach with a staff made from the Tree of
Life would lead to her pregnancy,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.400
and given that, I like how Rory is framed
in this shot with the Tree of Knowledge in

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.819
the stained glass window to her side.

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:24.849
Lucifer and Chloe's final moments together
on Earth as they ready themselves for him

00:03:24.849 --> 00:03:27.659
to go to Hell
will no doubt have been heart-breaking for

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:32.430
Deckerstar fans and even more so because this
scene mirrors the first time they met in the

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:33.459
Pilot.

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:35.540
"Lucifer Morningstar"?

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.500
Is that, uh, a stage name or something?

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.530
God-given, I'm afraid.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.870
So, um, Lucifer Morningstar...

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.680
Is that, like, a stage name or something?

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:46.120
God-given, I'm afraid.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.110
And when they play Heart and Soul together,
it's a tender call-back to the first time

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.319
they duetted with that song in Season 1.

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:57.189
I think you're gonna miss my incredible musical
prowess the most.

00:03:57.189 --> 00:04:02.129
Luci also played "Heart and Soul" in the third
season episode "Quintessential Deckerstar"

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:05.849
as a way to remind Chloe of their time together
before Pierce came along.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:10.900
And the Albanian field wench mention is also
a cute shout-out to the first season when

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.650
Chloe woke up in Lucifer's bed after getting
drunk the night before.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.090
You snore, by the way.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:18.579
Like an Albanian field wench!

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:22.710
Fortunately though, the sweet part of the
bittersweet ending promised by the showrunners

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.960
is still to come when decades later after
Chloe dies,

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:30.690
she goes to the afterlife and Amenadiel takes
her to Hell to reunite with Lucifer, proving

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.389
they really are partners to the end.

00:04:33.389 --> 00:04:34.389
Hello, Detective.

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:36.210
I thought you could use a partner.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:40.889
Lucifans will surely love that they got to
hear Lucifer call Chloe "detective" one final

00:04:40.889 --> 00:04:45.550
time, which neatly parallels the start of
the season when Luci called her by her name

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.490
and she replied:
'still not used to you calling me that.'

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:52.871
That very last time he calls her "detective"
is also a nice way of acknowledging that although

00:04:52.871 --> 00:04:57.560
Chloe gave up her police job at the end of
Season 5 so she could help Luci in his godly

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:00.520
duties,
being a detective was still very much part

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:01.520
of her DNA.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:07.250
And we saw that in the first episode of Season
6 when Chloe just couldn't stop herself investigating

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.720
the magician murder scene.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.610
Once the detective, always the detective.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:16.150
And remember this Deckerstar reunion in Hell
will be especially sweet for Lucifer given

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:20.120
that while decades have passed on earth between
Luci leaving and Chloe's death,

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.810
it's probably been hundreds of thousands if
not a few million years in Hell time for Lucifer.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:30.230
I love the fact that Lucifer's therapy room
in Hell appears to be a replica of Dr Linda's

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:33.740
office, proving just how great her influence
on him has been.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:37.650
And it's especially interesting that after
Luci counselled the good doctor in Season

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.419
5 on how she could reconcile with her daughter,
she told him this.

00:05:41.419 --> 00:05:43.110
Awfully insightful of you, Lucifer.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.139
Maybe you should become a therapist.

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:50.490
On Lucifer's couch in Hell is Reese, Linda's
ex-husband whose Hell Loop made up the Season

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.389
3 episode "Off The Record".

00:05:52.389 --> 00:05:57.270
Even now, Reese still can't break out of his
loop, but Lucifer is there diligently advising

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:01.080
him to confront his guilt head on rather than
avoiding it.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:06.600
And when Reese says he feels he's a lost cause,
Lucifer's reply sums up the show's key premise.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.259
Because if the devil can be redeemed, then
anyone can.

00:06:09.259 --> 00:06:14.160
Now, let's get into that final montage revealing
how everyone else ended up at the close of

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.160
the series.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:20.190
It begins in the Silver City with Amenadiel
taking his place as Amenagod, which many Lucifans

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:24.610
suspected would happen given his desire to
help people and how well suited he seems for

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:25.610
the position.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:30.099
After all, remember the advice about humanity
he gave Luci back in Season 4:

00:06:30.099 --> 00:06:33.099
Humans, Chloe, people are amazing.

00:06:33.099 --> 00:06:37.819
I'm only now just realizing how lucky we are...
that we actually get a chance to connect with

00:06:37.819 --> 00:06:38.819
them.

00:06:38.819 --> 00:06:42.629
And then there were his wonderful words to
Ella in Season 5 about her feelings that she

00:06:42.629 --> 00:06:44.389
didn't fully deserve God's love.

00:06:44.389 --> 00:06:49.220
You see, I think if God was standing right
here, right now, in front of you, that he

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.180
would tell you to take some of that faith
that you have in him...

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.620
and put it in yourself.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:58.479
And as it turns out Amenadiel's words foreshadowed
his rise to God status.

00:06:58.479 --> 00:07:03.020
Similar to his brother, Amenadiel also wants
to reform his part of the cosmos and make

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.500
Heaven a better place.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.229
I think every single angel should spend time
here..

00:07:07.229 --> 00:07:13.599
walking among humans, just like I did...
to get to really understand humanity.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:18.389
He also agreed with Lucifer to take joint
ownership of Lux and in the montage we see

00:07:18.389 --> 00:07:23.140
him gather his team of angels who he'll send
to work at Luci's club so they can mix with

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:24.879
all types of humans.

00:07:24.879 --> 00:07:28.919
And rather than operating in the mysterious
ways of their Father who left his family to

00:07:28.919 --> 00:07:34.310
work things out by themselves, Amenagod plans
to involve his angelic siblings in God's work

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:35.310
and keep them informed.

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:38.010
Being God...
...is what I truly desire.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:43.030
With Amenadiel now firmly in charge of Heaven,
the closing montage shows Ella caressing her

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:46.919
cross, her faith renewed as she senses the
big guy has returned.

00:07:46.919 --> 00:07:51.840
In some ways, Ella underwent perhaps the most
dramatic arc of all in the final season, as

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.990
she finally discovered the truth about her
celestial friends,

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:58.760
something teased all the way back in the "God
Johnson" episode of Season 2.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.379
Is it really so crazy?

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:03.300
I mean, what if God was one of us?

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:07.889
Many Lucifans were hoping Ella would find
out the truth, especially as in Season 5 she

00:08:07.889 --> 00:08:12.280
actually met God himself who helped her through
the darkness she was feeling at the time.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:15.010
The darker the darkness, the brighter the
light.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:18.470
And you, Miss Lopez, shine so very, very brightly.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.500
I can see it all the way from Heaven.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.240
Ella must have had a few suspicions before
then,

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.939
but God talking about seeing her from Heaven
and then disappearing mysteriously seems to

00:08:28.939 --> 00:08:33.730
have been the trigger for her secret investigation
and conspiracy board in Season 6.

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:38.080
And by the time of Maze and Eve's wedding,
Ella's suspicions are all but confirmed as

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:42.510
she sees Amenadiel talking to an invisible
Dan, and Carol comments about the strange

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:43.510
smell at the ceremony.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.510
What did you think?

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:48.710
What, we were at some, like, hell monster
wedding, attended by decaying zombies?

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:49.880
Ha ha!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:50.880
Hah!

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.920
At the afterparty, Ella can't take it anymore
and blurts out that she knows the truth.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:58.660
I know that Lucifer is the actual Devil!

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.750
Not, like, the most Method actor ever.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:06.080
That's a reference to what she said to Lucifer
when they first met in Season 2 and he told

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.080
her his name.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.080
Are you...

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.080
The Devil?

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:10.080
A method actor?

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.080
What?

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.080
Ugh.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.600
When Chloe confirms the truth to Ella, she's
not shocked because she already believed in

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:19.300
celestial beings, but she is angry with everyone
for excluding her from the club.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:24.041
But by the time Luci says farewell in the
next episode, Ella's now at peace, thanks

00:09:24.041 --> 00:09:27.550
to her chat with Carol, and understands why
they never told her.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:31.760
You don't have to know everything to have
trust.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:33.390
Not when you know each other's hearts.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:37.420
And given how many "happy" geeky T-shirts
we've seen Ella wear throughout the series,

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:41.750
I can't think of a better way to signal that
the young women's STEM foundation that Luci

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:46.360
established for her is up and running than
by showing her hand out those T-shirts.

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:51.270
The montage next shows Chloe returning to
the LAPD, part of the plan that she discussed

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:54.380
with Amenadiel to be God's point person in
the police department.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:59.500
Notice there's a time skip next, so when we
come back to Chloe we can see she's been promoted

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:03.320
and that she's taken the opportunity to promote
Officer Harris to detective.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:07.389
Hopefully, given the show's theme of growth,
Chloe is using the powers at her disposal

00:10:07.389 --> 00:10:11.190
now to change the system along with colleagues
like Harris.

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:15.811
Amenadiel even pops by to check in on things,
something that Harris seems to sense, as after

00:10:15.811 --> 00:10:18.000
all they had worked together.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:22.880
The montage also checks in on Dan who, as
so many of us expected, made it to Heaven

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:25.160
to be with his true love Charlotte Richards.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:30.589
And, of course, he gets to eat Pudding Plus,
which as we know from Season 3 is what Dan

00:10:30.589 --> 00:10:32.730
prefers:
Pudding Plus is my favorite, okay?

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.920
Twice as much protein as all the other brands.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:39.290
Some more fun details in this scene are the
"40 Whole Years of Being Dan" mug referencing

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:43.500
the time he was alive on Earth;
and the fact that Charlotte is getting waffles

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.540
for her heavenly treat is a call-back to the
waffle-maker that Dan bought her in Season

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.880
3 shortly before she was killed.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:54.589
In Season 6, we learn that the lingering guilt
holding Dan back from Heaven was his belief

00:10:54.589 --> 00:10:57.899
that he wasn't a good enough role model to
his daughter Trixie.

00:10:57.899 --> 00:11:01.420
When he goes to visit her in LeMec's body,
he confesses these feelings;

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:04.350
however, Trixie replies that he was the best
Dad ever.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.390
But he made so many mistakes.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:07.720
Everyone makes mistakes.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.360
And my dad taught me that mistakes are important.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:12.490
And we need them so that we can learn and...
do better next time.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:17.019
This is again the big theme of the whole series:
that there is always a path for anyone to

00:11:17.019 --> 00:11:18.019
redemption.

00:11:18.019 --> 00:11:22.640
And as Trixie tells Dan that she's proud of
her Dad, the guilt he feels washes away and

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:24.579
a light calls him up to Heaven.

00:11:24.579 --> 00:11:30.510
As the montage continues we get to see Charlie
celebrating his second birthday and, as predicted,

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:35.230
a set of wings pop out proving he has celestial
traits after all.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:39.710
Amenadiel gives a little punch in the air
as he's clearly delighted, as many Lucifans

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:40.780
will also be.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:45.730
Charlie being an angel also resolves the plot
point from Season 4 about why Remiel sensed

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.770
the birth of a new celestial on Earth.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:52.839
As to why Charlie's wings didn't show up until
now, it's likely because as a new-born he

00:11:52.839 --> 00:11:55.000
was too young to self-actualise.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:59.090
If that's the case, it seems Linda's attempts
to raise "the best child possible"

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:04.370
by giving baby Charlie access to an incredible
range of classes from Japanese to art appreciation

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:09.470
has paid off, helping him to develop and self-actualise
at a very young age.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:14.340
The montage also catches us up with everyone's
favourite demon, Maze, who turned down the

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:19.410
opportunity to rule Hell together with Eve,
a theory I mentioned back in Season 4.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:24.790
Instead, thanks to Linda's dinner table therapy,
Maze explains that rather than torturing souls

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:29.010
in Hell, what she really wants to do is to
carry on as a bounty hunter on Earth.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:32.220
It's so much better when they're still alive,
you know.

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:33.220
You can really feel the fear.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:37.779
During that dinner table session, Maze tells
Eve she's her true Hell, and so by the end

00:12:37.779 --> 00:12:41.589
we see they've found their bliss hunting down
and punishing perps,

00:12:41.589 --> 00:12:46.680
something Eve also enjoys as we saw how she
relished doing that with Luci in Season 4.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:51.230
Maze's farewell with Luci was exceptionally
emotional and when she gives him her demon

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:55.320
blade, it's especially significant because
her knives have been an integral part of her

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:57.180
since we first met her in Season 1.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:00.350
No matter what, you will always have a piece
of me.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:05.180
In fact, that demon blade is likely her last
one, as the other one was melted down at the

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:10.269
end of Season 5 to create the demon blade
bullets Chloe used in the celestial battle

00:13:10.269 --> 00:13:11.960
at the Olympic stadium.

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:16.730
The montage concludes with a phone call and
news that baby Rory has been born.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:21.110
And Maze's excitement at the knife gift she's
brought for the newly born babe reminds me

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:25.339
of the scene where she was showing Trixie
an assortment of weapons in Season 4 and slipped

00:13:25.339 --> 00:13:26.860
her a blade on the way out.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:29.720
Maze, you know she's not allowed to play with
knives.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.750
Relax, Dan, these knives aren't for Trixie.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:32.990
They're for a baby.

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:37.580
I thought the way the series wrapped up was
really well done and although it's been confirmed

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:42.459
this really is the final season,
it's nice to imagine that Lucifer and Chloe's

00:13:42.459 --> 00:13:45.430
story could continue in some form down in
Hell.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:50.410
They already both worked a case down there
in Season 6 when they investigated Jimmy Barnes's

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:51.410
Hell Loop.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:56.209
It's unlikely we'll be getting a Season 7
anytime soon, but other popular shows have

00:13:56.209 --> 00:14:01.670
been revived years later, and with the number
of resurrections this series has had already,

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:02.670
anything's possible!

